            <ArticleTitle>[Quantitative analysis of hemodynamic disorders in coronary occlusion based on the roentgeno-cinematographic data].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>28-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The contrasting time of the coronary arteries in 4 types of atherosclerotic lesions was determined by means of quantitative analysis of the coronarograms. The contrasting time was found to be dependent both on the degree of the stenosis and on the condition of the distal segment of the coronary artery. The condition of the drainage tracts had a more marked effect on the contrasting time. The coronary arteries contrasting time is considered as an index of peripheral resistance in the studied segment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
